@page "/docs/components/qr-code"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.QrCode
<PageTitle>QR Code - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">QR Code</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="qr-code" />
        </div>
        <p>A QR code rendered as pure SVG with no JavaScript, so it works in static SSR and scales without losing sharpness. It follows your theme colors by default, and you can change its colors, gradient, module and eye shapes, error correction, and add a logo or icon in the center.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(QrCodeUsageExample)"
                Description="Set `Value` to the text the code encodes, and use `Label` to say where it leads, since that becomes its accessible name." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Sizes" Description="`Size` has four presets. For any other size, pass your own size utilities through `Class`." Example="typeof(QrCodeSizesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Error correction"
          Description="Higher `ErrorCorrection` levels survive more damage or covering at the cost of a denser symbol. Use `High` when a logo sits in the center."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeErrorCorrectionExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Colors"
          Description="`Foreground` and `Background` take any CSS color, including theme tokens. By default the symbol follows the theme's foreground, but some readers struggle with light on dark, so set fixed colors when scanning must never fail."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeColorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Gradient"
          Description="Set `ForegroundEnd` for a two-stop linear gradient over the modules, and `GradientAngle` to change its direction. Keep both stops dark against the background, or scanners lose the lighter half."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeGradientExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Module styles" Description="`ModuleStyle` sets the shape of the data modules." Example="typeof(QrCodeModuleStylesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Eye styles"
          Description="`EyeStyle` shapes the three finder patterns, and `EyeColor` gives them their own color."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeEyesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Center image"
          Description="`ImageSrc` draws a logo in the middle. The modules underneath are cleared so it sits on a clean patch."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeImageExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Center content"
          Description="`CenterContent` renders your own markup in the middle instead, such as an icon or initials. `CenterScale` sets how much of the width it takes."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeCenterContentExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Quiet zone"
          Description="`QuietZone` is the blank margin around the symbol, measured in modules, so it scales with the code. The QR specification recommends 4 for difficult scanning conditions."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeQuietZoneExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Wi-Fi network"
          Description="A QR payload is a plain string. Here a `WIFI:` payload is built from the inputs as you type, and scanning the code joins the network."
          Example="typeof(QrCodeWifiExample)" />
</div>
